;; Known, explained disagreements between PostgreSQL 17.7 and pg-datahike
;; found by datahike.fuzz.differential. One entry per sample:
;;   {:surface :select|:prepared|:dml, :key <the SQL as generated>, :reason "..."}
;;
;; A disagreement NOT listed here fails the run (regression). A listed entry
;; that the run draws and that now AGREES also fails (baseline drift): prune
;; it and record the newly supported behaviour. Keep reasons specific --
;; "unsupported" is not a reason; say what is missing.
[{:surface :select
  :key "SELECT id, to_char(d, 'YYYY-MM-DD') AS c FROM ft ORDER BY id"
  :reason "to_char over date/timestamp is refused with 0A000: PostgreSQL's
           formatting.c template language (YYYY, MM, Day, FM, TH, ...) is not
           implemented. Numeric to_char works."}
 {:surface :join
  :key "SELECT count(*), count(fu.v) FROM ft FULL JOIN fu ON (ft.id = fu.id)"
  :reason "an aggregate over a FULL JOIN is refused with 0A000: the join is two\n           queries whose rows are concatenated, so an aggregate pushed into\n           the halves is computed per half and answered twice (count(*) said\n           5 and 4 where PostgreSQL says 7). Refused until the combination\n           happens before aggregation -- one query with two branches."}
